scenario the node that lost its fix stops being a second opinion
describe The mirror of scenario 17, on the half this device cannot check any
describe other way. There the receiver on the wrist lost its fix; here it is the
describe node. A receiver that loses its solution keeps sending the coordinate it
describe last solved for, so the relayed frame arrives looking exactly like an
describe answer, once a second, for as long as the dropout lasts.
describe
describe Three things followed from reading that shape as an answer, and each is
describe asserted below. A retained coordinate far from ours raised
describe `provider-disagreement` although the node had reported no fix at all —
describe and that reason alone scores 30, which is the default `degrade_at`. A
describe retained coordinate that happened to sit near ours cleared a live
describe allegation the node had never withdrawn. And the frames, arriving at
describe 1 Hz, kept restamping the anchor `provider_departure_grace` is measured
describe from, so the other side could never go quiet and the one exit this
describe reason has short of `provider_detached()` was unreachable.
describe
describe T-154 of ADR-0011 §5.2, issue #343.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted

# A real disagreement first, so what follows has something to be wrong about.
# The node has a fix of its own and puts us half a kilometre north of where our
# own receiver does. Both sides measured; both are claiming to know.
at 500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# Now the node loses its fix. The coordinate does not move — a field nobody
# rewrote keeps its old value — so this frame is byte-for-byte the accusation
# above with `fix none` in it. It is not one. What stands here is still the
# allegation the node made while it could answer, inside `evidence_ttl`.
at 1500
  fix none
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  provider other
  expect reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# Our own receiver is solving throughout — the dropout is the node's — and this
# fix is here so the local half of the comparison is inside
# `provider_comparison_window` when the next frame arrives. Without it the step
# below would pass for the wrong reason: it is this device that could not be
# compared, not the node that could not answer.
at 19500
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid

# Past `evidence_ttl`, and this is the assertion the defect fails. The only
# frames since have been retained coordinates half a kilometre out; if one of
# them counted as an answer it would have re-raised the reason and it would be
# live here. A node that has reported no fix at all accuses nobody. The device
# stays Degraded because the lapsed allegation is still awaited — nobody
# withdrew it — which is a different statement from the node making it again.
at 20000
  fix none
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

at 21000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

at 60000
  fix none
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# Two minutes after the last frame the node could answer with.
# `provider_departure_grace` has elapsed, so the allegation stops being awaited:
# a source that has stopped answering has stopped alleging. This is the step the
# defect could never reach — at 1 Hz every retained-coordinate frame above
# restamped the anchor the grace is measured from, so it never elapsed and the
# only exit short of `provider_detached()` was unreachable for the whole
# dropout.
at 121000
  fix none
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  provider other
  expect trust degraded

# `recover_hold` later, and one step at a time: Degraded climbs to Trusted.
at 127000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted

# The other half. A fresh, real disagreement — the node has its fix back and is
# still half a kilometre out.
at 127500
  fix 3d
  pos 5045000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 6000
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# And it drops out again, this time with a retained coordinate that happens to
# sit on top of ours. This is the shape that used to exonerate: a frame saying
# there is no position at all was read as the node agreeing with us, and the
# live allegation was retracted on its behalf. The node has withdrawn nothing,
# and the allegation is still live here.
at 128000
  fix none
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  provider other
  expect reason provider-disagreement
  expect trust degraded

# A withdrawal has to be measured. When the node solves again and agrees, the
# allegation goes — the gate narrows what counts as an answer, it does not stop
# the second source from ever clearing itself.
at 128500
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 9 12
  provider other
  expect no-reason provider-disagreement

at 134000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted
